# Upload ONLY what the Dockerfile uses. Everything else stays on this machine.
#
# Without this file gcloud falls back to .gitignore, which happens to keep .env out --
# but that is an implicit fallback, and the moment anyone adds a .gcloudignore without
# re-listing .env, secrets would start shipping to Cloud Build's storage bucket.
# A whitelist cannot fail that way: nothing uploads unless it is named here.
#
# The Dockerfile copies requirements.prod.txt and src/ -- nothing else.

*
!Dockerfile
!requirements.prod.txt
!src/
!src/**

# Even inside src/, never ship bytecode caches.
src/**/__pycache__/
